 "intro": [
  "The two and a half tribes that settled east of the Jordan. Reuben was the firstborn, \"but his birthright was given to the sons of Joseph,\" while \"Judah prevailed over his brothers and a ruler came from him\" (5:1–2). These tribes were the first to go into exile, carried off by Tiglath-pileser III of Assyria around 733 BC (5:6, 26).",
  "Most names are clan leaders recorded in the reigns of Jotham and Jeroboam II (5:17). Dashed lines mark families whose link is not given."
 ],
 "sources": "Hebrew names: Miqra according to the Masorah. Scholarly summary after the standard commentaries (Japhet; Williamson; Knoppers).",
